  "notes": "A godan verb compound of {出|だ}す (to put out) and {抜|ぬ}く (to pull out, to surpass). Carries a negative connotation of using cunning or underhandedness to get ahead of others. Often used in business and competitive contexts.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive — takes を to mark the person being outsmarted.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ライバルを{出|だ}し{抜|ぬ}く — to outsmart a rival\n- {人|ひと}を{出|だ}し{抜|ぬ}く — to get the better of someone\n- {出|だ}し{抜|ぬ}かれる — to be outsmarted (passive)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {裏|うら}をかく — to outwit, to catch off guard\n- {先手|せんて}を{打|う}つ — to make the first move (more neutral)\n- {騙|だま}す — to deceive, to trick (more directly dishonest)",
